It is Thursday evening.
I am at the hairdresser at half past seven.
The hairdresser greets me warmly.
"Good evening, Frau Flores," she says.
"Here is your seat."
I sit on the chair and look in the mirror.
"I would like my hair short, please," I say.
The hairdresser washes my hair first.
Then she cuts my hair.
She works very well.
I do not go to the hairdresser every month.
Sometimes I only go in the summer.
But today I need a new style.
The hairdresser is soon finished.
"How do you like it?" she asks.
I look in the mirror again.
"That is great, thank you very much," I answer.
I say goodbye and go outside.
I walk back to my flat.
I am ready for the weekend!
